
GROUP PROJECT (35% of total marks I 'm doing resort facts and background only)
Students are required to form a group of 5-6 members to evaluate ONE type of resort hotel covered in this subject.
You will take on the role of a consulting team for a resort (located outside Hong Kong and Macau) and conduct an analysis and evaluation of its facilities and services based on the following areas:
1. Resort facts and background, including accommodation, food and beverage outlets, public areas, and leisure or recreational facilities.
2. Design principles and guidelines applied within the resort.
3. Target market segments.
4. Impacts on industry stakeholders arising from the resort's facilities, planning, and development
5. A specialised topic relevant to the specific type of resort you have selected (bonus mark component)
Your work should go beyond simply presenting the factual information. You are expected to apply relevant concepts, provide critical evaluations, and offer well-reasoned recommendations based on your analysis. Demonstrating creativity and strong critical thinking will be essential to showcasing your capability in this project.
The written report should not exceed 3,000 words, excluding cover page, executive summary, reference materials, and appendices (if any). It should be in MS Word on page A4 with font size 12; Times New Roman; 1.5 line spacing: 1" margins all round.
Students should submit a SOFT copy (via email) of the written project report to the Subject Lecturer before the due date/time. NO late submission will be accepted under any
circumstances.
In addition to the written report, each group will have 25-30 minutes to present their findings plus another 5-7 minutes question and answer session with the audience. Presentation schedules for group projects will be confirmed in class with consent from all groups in due course.


